  {
    "id": "3809819cc4ad6f82f206",
    "source": "Concentration is server-tracked: the tool that casts a concentration spell sets it (and reports any previous spell it displaced), damage triggers the CON save automatically with the result in the apply_damage response, and dropping to 0 HP ends it. A caster ending concentration on purpose is clear_condition with \"concentration\". Narrate concentration only from what the tools report, and honor a reported break: that casting's effects end immediately, and only that casting's. A player's own cast that ends their running concentration spell reaches you already confirmed (the table asked them first), so cast it. When a player asks an AI companion to cast a concentration spell while that companion holds a different one, the companion first says which spell would end and waits for that player's yes before any casting tool; a request that already says to drop the running spell needs no second question, and a companion's own choices on its turn need none.",
    "sourceHash": "3809819cc4ad6f82f206c6e389c6f1574ee18a2539984763d1ac9e3554e345f7",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
